WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.872
[MUSIC]

00:00:07.872 --> 00:00:11.137
A lot of the communication that's going on
with Twitter is

00:00:11.137 --> 00:00:13.611
the simple dissemination of information.

00:00:13.611 --> 00:00:16.811
If a firm has some news they want to get
out to the markets,

00:00:16.811 --> 00:00:20.770
they use a tweet to tweet the information
and a link to it.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.810
And then the question is, does this have
an effect?

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.323
Does this improve the information
environment of the firm?

00:00:25.323 --> 00:00:28.159
[MUSIC]

00:00:28.159 --> 00:00:29.712
We look at these firms, and

00:00:29.712 --> 00:00:33.898
we examine when they tweet versus when
they don't tweet, and we find that

00:00:33.898 --> 00:00:39.260
when they choose to tweet an event, that
the market liquidity's actually improved.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:43.180
We see bid ask spreads narrow, and we see
the depths widen.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:47.060
And more importantly, we see this effect
as being stronger for

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.300
those firms that you would call less
visible, those that might have

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.590
trouble getting attention from the
traditional media outlets.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:57.570
So it'd be firms that are smaller, firms
that have fewer shareholders,

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.380
firms that have fewer institutions looking
at them.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:04.328
These firms are the ones that have more
trouble getting their message out.

00:01:04.328 --> 00:01:07.138
And Twitter is a channel that they can use
to

00:01:07.138 --> 00:01:10.268
more broadly disseminate their
information.

00:01:10.268 --> 00:01:13.204
[MUSIC]

00:01:13.204 --> 00:01:16.820
My first advice would be to definitely
take it seriously.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.119
A lot of these new technologies, it's easy
to dismiss because it's not the way that

00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:24.150
you've done things in the past, and it's
not the, the traditional,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.160
normal way of communicating with
investors, but as we show in our study,

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:31.780
Twitter can be extremely helpful for firms
that are using it.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.950
Especially if they can't get attention
from the traditional media outlets.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.890
This is a new channel, this is a new way
of communicating.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:41.150
And it does impact the firm's information
environment.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.925
It helps their market liquidity.

00:01:42.925 --> 00:01:47.460
S, my advise would be to look at Twitter
or look at Facebook.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.070
Or look at these different technologies
and see what's right for your firm.

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:54.980
Think about what your goals are and what
you want to accomplish.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:55.696
And work, and

00:01:55.696 --> 00:01:59.951
think about how these tools might help you
better communicate with your investors.

00:01:59.951 --> 00:02:02.887
[MUSIC]

00:02:02.887 --> 00:02:06.620
The way that firms are communicating with
investors, it's changing.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:11.800
Whether firms want it to or not, the
advent of new technology coming in and

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.848
different venues for them to interact
with.

00:02:13.848 --> 00:02:18.450
It's changing investors' expectations, and
it's changing the possibilities for firms.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:22.741
So the exciting thing is that firms, they
can choose to embrace this.

00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:25.843
And they can start to see some real
benefits coming from it.

00:02:25.843 --> 00:02:35.459
[MUSIC]

